  nonce: '64e2'  # 64e2
  message: "Fixed in PR #1260 (cb7aa60f83). load/start/stop/ensure_started/ensure_all_started moved from env_write to process_send: read in OTP's kernel source (application.erl / application_controller.erl), each is a gen_server call into the application controller process (load_application / start_application / stop_application -> call(...)), the class gen_server:call already has. The .app resource file is read inside the controller, not at the call site, so no fs_read row. set_env/unset_env stay env_write under the INV-nular ruling. Behavioural evidence on merged dev, the 09-27 fixture through hypergumbo io-boundaries --format json (cold cache): env_write = {application.set_env} only (was 6 chains incl. the five lifecycle functions); process_send = load, ensure_all_started, ensure_started, start, stop. Pinned by test_erlang_application_lifecycle.py. NOT changed: application's host_info_read row (get_application / loaded_applications / which_applications / info), which are also controller calls; outside this item."  # 64e2
